// kyoten::input::Digital — an action a processor reads as on or off (components § Decided, step 5 question 6). An
// action's kind names the value a processor reads, not a device, so one `Digital` serves a key, a button, a trigger
// past a threshold and a UI button.
//
// Each field of a game's generated `Actions` holds one, filled by the Input phase from the player the entity names
// (KYR-54, step 8), and a processor reads it through `const ref Actions`: `if (input.faster.held) { … }`. How
// `pressed` and `released` are set across steps, rate gating included, is step 8's.

export { Digital };

type value Digital {
    // On this step.
    public bool held = false;
    // On this step, and off the step before.
    public bool pressed = false;
    // Off this step, and on the step before.
    public bool released = false;

    // Off, as every action is before its first input.
    public default ctor off() { }
}
